* ============================================================================
* 02_csv_to_dbf_v2.dts   --  CSV -> DBF with type inference, runnable
*
* Replaces 02_csv_to_dbf_students.dts, which could not execute:
*   IMPORT CSV <f> SCHEMA <json> REJECTS <csv>
*     -> IMPORT grammar is IMPORT <csvfile> only. No SCHEMA or REJECTS options.
*   USE students_import
*     -> IMPORT APPENDS INTO THE ALREADY-OPEN TABLE. It never creates a table,
*        so students_import would never exist. Creating a table from a CSV is
*        AUTODBF's job, not IMPORT's. This is the substantive correction: the
*        original conflated two different commands.
*   _drops/ -> does not exist; TMP does.
*
* This test proves the CSV -> x64base direction INCLUDING type inference, which
* is the part that actually matters. A row count alone would pass even if every
* column collapsed to character.
* ============================================================================

SET TALK ON
ECHO CONV02 BEGIN csv-to-dbf

ECHO CONV02 LOAD
AUTODBF X64 CONVERSION_CSV_TO_DBF_ITEMS_V1 FROM cascade_precision_erp/data/Items.csv HEADER INFER OVERWRITE

ECHO CONV02 VERIFY
USE CONVERSION_CSV_TO_DBF_ITEMS_V1
COUNT
STRUCT

* -- the two behaviours worth asserting explicitly -----------------------------
* Both were derived from src/import/import_profile.cpp and confirmed by run on
* 2026-07-26. They are the tripwires: if either changes, the inference ladder or
* its ordering changed underneath the migration story.
ECHO CONV02 TRIPWIRE list-price-must-be-N-despite-14-empties
ECHO CONV02 TRIPWIRE active-must-be-N-not-L
ECHO CONV02 NULLCHECK
LOCATE FOR SKU = "RAW-SHAFT-4140"
DISPLAY

ECHO CONV02 END

* ============================================================================
* PASS CRITERIA  (derived, not estimated -- see 10_crosswalk_cascade_items_v1.dts)
*   COUNT       = 18
*   field count = 13
*   type letters, in order:  N C C C C C N N N N N C N
*     ITEM_ID N . SKU C . DESCRIPTION C . UOM C . ITEM_TYPE C . COST_METHOD C
*     STANDARD_COST N . LIST_PRICE N . REORDER_POINT N . REORDER_QTY N
*     LEAD_DAYS N . CATEGORY C . ACTIVE N
*
*   LIST_PRICE  = N   even though 14 of 18 cells are empty.
*                     update_profile() returns on empty before setting any
*                     category flag, so empties cannot force MIXED.
*   ACTIVE      = N   NOT L. is_logical_text() accepts "1"/"0", but
*                     update_profile() tests is_integer_text() FIRST and returns,
*                     making the LOGICAL branch unreachable for numeric literals.
*   NULLCHECK   LIST_PRICE renders EMPTY, not 0.
*
* FAIL means any type letter differs, or LIST_PRICE shows 0 instead of blank.
* A matching row count is NOT sufficient.
* ============================================================================
